            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0181" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.811/1002: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-24T16:00:00-04:00">August 24, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following for Tokyo: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>296. “Shanghai’s 1152, August 22, 7 p.m., in regard to Whangpoo
                            Conservancy Board. The Department desires that, after consultation with
                            your British and French colleagues, and if and when they are prepared to
                            take separate but similar action, you approach the Japanese Foreign
                            Office, in such manner as you may deem appropriate, substantially along
                            the lines indicated in paragraph 1 of the telegram under reference.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeat to Chungking and mail copy to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
